    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d115">

                <pb facs="0225" n="109" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg109"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 893.811/129.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chinese Minister to the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 6.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Chinese Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-05-23">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 23, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to the board of engineers
                    to be composed of Colonel William L. Sibert as chief and Mr. Arthur P. Davis and
                    Professor D. W. Mead to proceed to China to make a supplementary examination of
                    the Hwai River region, I am authorized by my instructions to say that the
                    Government of the Republic of China desires the board to come to China at as
                    early a date as possible.</p>
                <p>I have already had the pleasure of informing my Government by cable of the
                    designation of Colonel Sibert as chief of the board.</p>
                <p>Accept [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Kai Fu Shah</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
